title: 'TODO : generalize an atom''s ''contains'' from list to tree'
pid: cc80de91-36b0-4f32-8a31-c85bdc583ac9
body: |2-
  An atom A's 'contains' could look like this:
  - X
  - Y
  - Z
  -- Z' which Z contains
  --- Z'' which Z' contains
  -- W which Z does not contain

  When A recursively presents, those things it contains will be heralded differently:
  some are presented by more ancestors than others.
